  "worked_solution": "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$8$** | **$16$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** | **$10$** |\n| ${x}_{3}$ | **$-10$** | **$-8$** | **$-5$** | **$-1$** | **$2$** |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $10$ | $16$ | $22$ | $30$ |\n\n \n\nThe coefficients of the hyperplane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}_{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 16 & 10 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 22 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.",
